-- title:
--   Degree p-1 of the diamond cover X₁(Mp)→ X_{Γ_1(M)∩Γ_0(p)}
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero (hence a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra). Inside the field $L((q))$ of formal Laurent series over $L$, consider two intermediate fields $K$ and $K_1$ over $L$, subject to the following descriptions. The field $K$ is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image, under the map $L((q)) \hookleftarrow \mathbb{Q}((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137), that is of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the set [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83); the field $K_1$ is the $L$-subfield generated in the same way by the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield generated by [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 M ⊓ Gamma0 p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83). Assume further $K_1 \le K$. Then the relative degree `IntermediateField.relfinrank K₁ K`, which under this inclusion is the degree $[K : K_1]$, equals $p - 1$ (truncated subtraction of natural numbers).
--
--   This is the degree of the covering $X_1(Mp) \to X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ cut out by the diamond operators at $p$, expressed on the $q$-expansion function fields base changed to an arbitrary field of characteristic zero; on the group side it reflects the index $[\pm(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)) : \pm\Gamma_1(Mp)] = p - 1$. It is used in the analysis of valuation subrings and uniformisers on the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over its $\Gamma_0(p)$-floor, and as the degree part of the corresponding cyclic-Galois statement for the same cover.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_relfinrank_eq_sub_one_x1FunctionField_mul_x1x0.lean

